 "draw the load order for a nested working directory and prove it with /context.",
 "know which file a line lives in before you edit; the level decides who it affects.",
 "files are concatenated, not overridden, so a lower-level file cannot delete a higher-level rule; it can only add to it [Claude Code docs, Memory, 2026].",
 22, "2", ["List the four locations and their sharing", "Predict what loads for a working directory and verify", "Design the layering for a monorepo and a managed rollout"],
